# Keystores — never commit signing keys
*.jks
*.keystore
# Exception: Google Sign-In binds to the signing certificate's SHA-1, and CI
# generates a fresh debug key on every run, which would break sign-in with
# each new build. This one key is committed so the fingerprint is stable.
# It signs a sideloaded personal build only — never publish with it. To use a
# private key instead, add the repo secret SIGNING_KEYSTORE_BASE64 (and
# SIGNING_PASSWORD); the workflow prefers the secret when it is present.
!keystore/notes.keystore

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
